In the case at hand, facts are distinctive in the sense, victim is first cousin sister of the appellant.
At the relevant time, she was 15 year old and appellant was 19 year old.
Both were students and living in one house.
A fact cannot be overlooked that the victim had resiled from her statement and further disowned the contents of portion marked B of her statement recorded under Section 164.
Even her mother was unfriendly to prosecution.
The FSL report was not obtained till the conclusion of the trial.
Victim said, her statement to the police and narrative in statement under Section 164 was at the instance of Class teacher.
Therefore, in the proceedings, wherein suspension of sentence is sought, this Court cannot ignore the evidence of victim and her mother.
At the same time, the age of the victim and of appellant their relations also cannot be overlooked.
